Apple's rumored all-glass iPhone expected to mark the device's 20th anniversary has been canceled, according to Jefferies analyst Edison Lee.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/iphone-20-anniversary.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1057094" /><br/>
Rumors have circulated since at least 2025 that Apple was developing a radically redesigned all-glass iPhone, with launch expected as early as September 2027. Lee's analysis today provided in <a href="https://www.barrons.com/articles/apple-stock-sell-downgrade-iphone-glass-2a001a49"><em>Barron's</em></a> claims that his firm's supply chain checks now point to the project being scrapped due to poor production yield, the rate at which manufacturing produces defect-free units.<br/>
<br/>
As a result of the findings, Jefferies downgraded Apple stock to "Underperform," the equivalent of a "Sell" rating, from "Hold" today, cutting its price target to &#36;263.66 from &#36;285.56, one of the lowest on Wall Street. Apple shares fell 2.1% following the downgrade.<br/>
<br/>
The all-glass iPhone has been <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/22/2027-iphone-dramatic-redesign/">rumored for well over a year</a> as the most significant redesign since the iPhone X, expected to arrive in fall 2027 alongside a second-generation foldable iPhone. Reports pointed to a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/05/12/20th-anniversary-iphone-all-screen-design/">curved glass panel</a> wrapping around the front and back with virtually no cutouts in the display, along with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/08/iphone-18-pro-under-display-face-id/">under-display Face ID</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/28/20th-anniversary-iphone-solid-state-buttons/">solid-state buttons</a>. <br/>
<br/>
<ul><li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/29/20th-anniversary-iphone-10-features/">20th Anniversary iPhone Coming Next Year With These 10 Features</a></li></ul><br/>
<br/>
Lee previously viewed the all-glass iPhone as a plausible upcoming release, and its apparent cancellation changes his view of Apple's ability to raise iPhone prices going forward. He called the move a major setback for pushing higher-priced iPhones as memory costs continue to climb. Had it launched in 2027, Lee estimated the device would have carried a blended retail price of around &#36;2,060, higher than any previous iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
The bigger concern for Lee is what the cancellation means beyond a single model. He believes Apple had planned to eventually bring all-glass styling to the iPhone Pro and Pro Max lines as well, in a move he saw as a way to further raise those models' average selling price and margin at a time when rising memory costs are squeezing profitability.<br/>
<br/>
Lee also pointed to Apple's AI strategy and rising component costs for the "iPhone 19 Pro Max," expected in 2027, as additional reasons behind the downgrade. The slow rollout of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a>, he argued, makes it harder for Apple to justify equipping more iPhones with the extra RAM needed to run AI models on-device.<br/>
<br/>
It remains unclear whether Lee is describing the end of the entire 20th-anniversary redesign or just its all-glass display component. It has repeatedly been <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/01/22/20th-anniversary-iphone-all-screen-design-in-doubt/">questioned</a> whether Apple can eliminate the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a> next year at all, given the engineering hurdles involved, meaning a genuinely seamless glass front may never have been realistic regardless of Lee's yield and cost concerns. Even so, other elements of the rumored 20th anniversary design, including the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/24/20th-anniversary-iphone-micro-curved-oled-panel/">quad-curved chassis</a>, could still be on track.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/20th-anniversary-iphone/">20th-Anniversary iPhone</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/aapl/">AAPL</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/barrons-com/">Barron's</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/10/all-glass-20th-anniversary-iphone-canceled/">Apple&#039;s All-Glass 20th Anniversary iPhone Reportedly Canceled</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apples-all-glass-20th-anniversary-iphone-reportedly-canceled.2486679/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>